                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentInstanceProperties>
                    <name>richTextValue</name>
                    <value>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Objection Category Definitions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Choose the one category that fits each objection best, and put the detail in the notes.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Patient Access: &lt;/strong&gt;The care itself was blocked or delayed. This covers anything that stopped a patient being seen, scanned or treated when they needed to be, including no availability, waits beyond what is clinically reasonable, an inability to reach scheduling, urgency that was not honored, referrals that never became a scheduled appointment, and patients turned away at the point of service. Choose this when the problem is that the care did not happen, or happened too late.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication: &lt;/strong&gt;Information did not reach the person who needed it, or reached them wrong. This covers results and updates never passed on, calls and messages that went unanswered, referrals whose outcome the sender was never told, conflicting or incorrect information given to an office or a patient, and orders and instructions that were misunderstood. Choose this when the care may have been fine but someone was left uninformed or misinformed.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Records: &lt;/strong&gt;A document, result or record did not arrive, or could not be retrieved when it was needed. This covers clinical documentation that does not flow back to a referring office, transmission failures in either direction, reports that remain unavailable after the service was delivered, and records that arrive incomplete, unreadable, or attached to the wrong patient or provider. Choose this when the problem is the record itself rather than a conversation about it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Patient Experience: &lt;/strong&gt;The patient or family was treated poorly, separate from whether the care took place. This covers staff conduct and courtesy, care that felt disjointed across departments, unexpected or inconsistent cost conversations at the point of service, concerns about the quality of the encounter, and the physical experience of getting through the visit. Choose this when the complaint is about how it felt rather than whether it happened.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Insurance:&lt;/strong&gt; Coverage, benefits or authorization stood in the way. This covers prior authorizations that were delayed, denied or never submitted, plans incorrectly reported as not accepted, plans we genuinely do not contract with, and cost or payment terms that stopped a patient proceeding. Choose this when the obstacle was the plan or the authorization rather than capacity or communication.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network Access: &lt;/strong&gt;The referring practice cannot connect to us, or what they need does not exist in their market. This covers system access that was never granted or has stopped working, connectivity between their systems and ours, providers and services that cannot be found when someone tries to refer, and gaps where no in network option exists nearby. Choose this when the practice is unable to reach or use Orlando Health at all, rather than having a problem with one specific patient.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Locations:&lt;/strong&gt; Where the care is delivered is the problem. This covers distance and travel that patients will not or cannot undertake, services available only at a site further away than the patient needs, the absence of a nearby facility of the right type, and the condition or accessibility of the building itself. Choose this when the issue would be solved by delivering the same care somewhere else.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</value>
                </componentInstanceProperties>
                <componentName>flexipage:richText</componentName>
                <identifier>flexipage_richText</identifier>
            </componentInstance>
        </itemInstances>
